---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { editorialProfile } from "../data/editorial";
---

<BaseLayout title="Editorial Review" description="Who publishes Kreativ Auto, how reviewed guides are researched, and how corrections are handled." modifiedTime={new Date("2026-09-01")} enableAds={false}>
  <div class="container-shell py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="surface hero-frame p-8 sm:p-10">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <p class="eyebrow">Editorial review</p>
        <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">Who is responsible for the guides</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-8 text-steel">
          {editorialProfile.name} is the publisher and editor of Kreativ Auto and is responsible for the site's editorial direction, source selection, page updates, and corrections process.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-steel">
          The site does not claim that its editor is a mechanic, has personally inspected every vehicle, or has tested every product. Published manufacturer and regulator material is kept distinct from editorial judgment about the next sensible check.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-10 surface p-6 sm:p-8">
      <p class="eyebrow">Named accountability</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">Who is accountable for a published page</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
        <article class="editorial-card"><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Publisher and editor</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">Andrei Olaru is identified on published editorial bylines and is responsible for the final wording, source selection, scope, and visible review date.</p></article>
        <article class="editorial-card"><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">What is not claimed</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">A byline does not claim mechanic credentials, personal ownership, road testing, vehicle inspection, or product testing unless that evidence is stated and available on the page.</p></article>
        <article class="editorial-card"><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Corrections contact</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">Send the page URL, affected statement, and supporting source or vehicle detail to <a class="font-semibold text-accent hover:underline" href="mailto:info@kreativauto.com">info@kreativauto.com</a>.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 surface p-6 sm:p-8">
      <p class="eyebrow">Review standard</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">What an indexed guide must show</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
        <article class="editorial-card">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Vehicle scope</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">The model year, generation, engine, drivetrain, and market assumptions are stated where they materially change the answer.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="editorial-card">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Traceable sources</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">Maintenance, recall, safety, and specification claims are checked against manufacturer or regulator material and linked in the guide's sources and scope section.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="editorial-card">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Useful limits</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">A guide distinguishes published source material from editorial judgment and does not claim workshop testing, vehicle inspection, or personal ownership that did not occur.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="editorial-card">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Commercial restraint</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">Parts pages remain out of search until their fitment, selection criteria, alternatives, source links, and disclosure meet the same standard.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 surface p-6 sm:p-8">
      <p class="eyebrow">Attribution</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">What the byline means</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
        <article class="editorial-card">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Editor responsibility</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">A byline identifies who is accountable for the wording, source selection, scope, links, and visible update date. It does not imply an unlisted qualification or hands-on test.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="editorial-card">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Source responsibility</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">A linked manufacturer, retailer, or regulator is cited for its own published information. It is not treated as an endorsement of Kreativ Auto's interpretation or a substitute for an individual vehicle inspection.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 surface p-6 sm:p-8">
      <p class="eyebrow">Corrections</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">How a correction is handled</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
        <p>Send the page URL, the affected statement, and the source or vehicle detail that needs review to <a class="font-semibold text-accent hover:text-ink" href="mailto:info@kreativauto.com">info@kreativauto.com</a>.</p>
        <p>Corrections are checked against the cited source, the page's stated vehicle scope, and related reviewed guidance. Material editorial changes receive an updated review date.</p>
        <p>When a source is withdrawn, a link stops supporting the claim, or a product listing no longer provides adequate fitment detail, the relevant recommendation can be narrowed, removed, or kept out of search until it is reviewed again.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
